This document is a draft framework for future paid Enterprise offerings.
It does not grant rights by itself until a signed agreement is executed.

1. Community Edition (MIT — see LICENSE)
   The open-source Community Edition already includes, under the MIT License:
   - Single-pair GUI / CLI comparison
   - Excel + HTML/PDF reports and 4 languages (TR / RU / DE / EN)
   - Folder / batch comparison (`--batch`)
   - SQLite result archive (`--archive`)
   Community Edition remains free to use, modify, and redistribute under MIT.

2. Scope of Enterprise (planned, paid)
   Enterprise offerings may add commercial value on top of Community, for example:
   - Signed Windows binaries and installers
   - Priority support / SLA
   - Corporate deployment packaging and volume licensing
   - Optional hosted / multi-seat management (if offered)

   Batch comparison, SQLite archive, and HTML/PDF reports are NOT reserved
   exclusively for Enterprise — they ship in Community under MIT.

3. Grant
   Upon payment and a signed order form / license agreement, the Licensor
   grants the Licensee a non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the
   Enterprise Edition according to the seat / site / volume terms stated in
   that agreement.

4. Restrictions
   Unless expressly allowed in the signed agreement, the Licensee may not:
   - Redistribute Enterprise binaries or license keys
   - Remove or bypass license checks
   - Use Enterprise features beyond the purchased capacity

5. Warranty and liability
   Commercial warranty and liability caps are defined only in the signed
   agreement. This draft provides no warranty. Community Edition remains
   under the MIT License disclaimer.

6. Contact
   For Enterprise licensing inquiries, open a GitHub Discussion or contact
   the repository maintainers.

This draft may be replaced by a formal agreement without notice.
